 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Complexity:** The computational cost is dominated by the numerical integration of the volume rendering integral. It requires evaluating transmittance, extinction, and phase functions at each sample point along the ray.
-*   **Strengths:** Simple analytical form for idealized active illumination scenarios; correctly models inverse-square falloff and double-pass attenuation.
-*   **Limitations:** Invalid for scenes with significant ambient light or forward scattering in participating media. Assumes the camera and light are at the exact same position.
